{"name":"Gun Corps Brown","hex":"#6b593c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mbya Guarani."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device for shooting projectiles or ditto (a shooter), functioning through stored energy: a firearm, cannon, harpoon gun/spear gun, raygun, etc, not a bow and arrow, or slingshot.","A very portable, short firearm, for hand use, which fires bullets or projectiles, such as a handgun, revolver, pistol, or Derringer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gun"},{"term":"corps","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A battlefield formation composed of two or more divisions.","An organized group of people united by a common purpose."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A corps de ballet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corps"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gun","blocks":[{"text":"A gun is a device that propels a projectile using pressure or explosive force. The projectiles are typically solid, but can also be pressurized liquid, or gas. Solid projectiles may be free-flying or tethered. A large-caliber gun is also called a cannon, while a hand-held gun may be called a firearm. Guns were designed as weapons for military use, and then found use in hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg/330px-SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun","wikidata":"Q110155210"},{"title":"Corps","blocks":[{"text":"Corps is a term used for several different kinds of 